cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, discuss, or build on TinyAMP, please cite this software and the APD dataset used by the project."
title: "TinyAMP: Exploring data, model capacity, and generalization in a small peptide language model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Xie"
    given-names: "Steven"
version: "2.0.0"
abstract: >-
  TinyAMP is a small decoder-only peptide language model implemented directly
  in PyTorch and trained from random initialization on natural antimicrobial
  peptide sequences. The project studies sequence context, similarity-aware
  train/test splitting, model-capacity scaling, overfitting, dropout,
  training-data scaling, repeated-seed variability, and generated-sequence
  similarity and diversity.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial peptides
  - peptide language model
  - transformer
  - PyTorch
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - sequence modeling
  - autoregressive model
